## Data Models & Protocol

### Sensor Metadata (Backend → Frontend)

```python
# models/descriptors.py
from pydantic import BaseModel
from typing import Literal, List, Optional

SensorKind = Literal["EEG", "ECG", "GSR", "HR", "ACCEL", "OTHER"]

class ChannelInfo(BaseModel):
    id: str
    label: str
    unit: Optional[str] = None

class SensorDescriptor(BaseModel):
    id: str                    # e.g. "eeg_muse", "gsr_teensy"
    name: str                  # Human-readable name
    kind: SensorKind
    channels: List[ChannelInfo]
    sampling_rate: float
    backend: str               # e.g. "lsl", "serial"
    enabled: bool
```

### Sample Batches (Backend → Frontend, configurable rate)

```python
# models/messages.py
class SampleBatch(BaseModel):
    deviceId: str
    timestamp: float           # Unix seconds for first sample
    channels: List[str]        # Channel IDs
    samplingRate: float
    values: List[List[float]]  # shape: [n_samples][n_channels]

class SamplesMessage(BaseModel):
    type: Literal["samples"] = "samples"
    payload: List[SampleBatch]
```

### State Estimates (Backend → Frontend, 1 Hz)

```python
# state/estimator.py
class StateScores(BaseModel):
    focus: float       # 0–1
    stress: float      # 0–1
    relaxation: float  # 0–1

class StateEstimate(BaseModel):
    type: Literal["state"] = "state"
    timestamp: float
    scores: StateScores
    label: Optional[str] = None
    explanation: Optional[str] = None
```

### Control Messages (Frontend → Backend)

```typescript
// api/messageTypes.ts
type ControlMessage =
  | { type: 'control'; action: 'enable' | 'disable'; deviceId: string }
  | { type: 'audio_event'; event: 'start' | 'stop'; trackId: string; trackName?: string };
```

